        '3-5', $q$From Egg to Frog$q$, $q$(1) Frogs change a lot as they grow. (2) Most frogs begin life as tiny eggs in the water. (3) Many kinds of frogs lay hundreds of eggs at one time.

(4) A tadpole hatches from each egg. (5) A tadpole is a young frog that lives in the water and has a long tail. (6) It breathes through gills, like a fish does. (7) My brother has a pet goldfish named Bubbles.

(8) Slowly, the tadpole grows two back legs. (9) ___ it grows two front legs. (10) Its tail gets shorter and shorter. (11) It also grows lungs so it can breathe air.

(12) At last, the young frog hops out of the water onto land.$q$, 'draft')
