values ('35b8da7e-1924-5b92-a6cb-8b643b8bada0', 'wg3-informative-writing-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g3-informative-writing'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Camels in the Desert$q$, $q$(1) Camels are animals that live in dry deserts, where water is hard to find. (2) They can walk for many days across the sand.

(3) Many people think a camel's hump is full of water. (4) ___ the hump is really filled with fat. (5) A camel's body can use this fat for energy when food is hard to find.

(6) Camels have body parts that help them live in the desert. (7) Their long eyelashes keep blowing sand out of their eyes. (8) They can close their nostrils when the wind blows sand. (9) Their wide feet help them walk on soft sand without sinking.

(10) Camels can go a long time without drinking water. (11) When they find water, they can drink a lot of it very quickly. (12) My family went to the beach last summer, and the sand there was very hot.$q$, 'draft')
