        '3-5', $q$The Wobbly Skater$q$, $q$(1) Last Saturday, my aunt took me ice skating for the very first time. (2) The rink was bright and cold, and music played from speakers on the walls. (3) I laced up my rented skates and stepped onto the ice. (4) My feet slid in two different directions right away! (5) I grabbed the wall so hard that my fingers hurt.

(6) Aunt Rosa skated over and held out her hand. (7) "Bend your knees and take tiny steps," she said. (8) I tried it, but I still fell down twice. (9) My cheeks felt hot because I thought everyone was watching me. (10) Then I saw a little boy fall, laugh, and get right back up. (11) After that, I kept trying too.

(12) By the end of the afternoon, I could skate all the way around the rink without the wall. (13) The snack bar sold popcorn and hot cocoa.$q$, 'draft')
